  "prefLabel": "Fis 601.04 Net",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Fis 601.04 “Net” means any open fabric constructed of materials such as but not limited to string, cord, thread, or wire, knotted or woven together in such a way as to be capable of entraining or entrapping fin fish.\n\nSource. #1670, eff 11-20-80; ss by #2263, eff 1-7-83; ss by #2839, eff 8-31-84; ss by #4868, eff 7-20-90; ss by #6291, eff 7-20-96; ss by #8087, eff 5-27-04; ss by #10095, eff 2-29-12; ss by #12652, eff 10-27-18 (formerly Fis 601.02)",
